<blockquote class="uncited"><div> I use Bullet physics 2.82 and Detours Library ( last version) and trying compile your Crowd demo [...]</div></blockquote>The Detour and DetourCrowd libraries are not necessary, because their source code is included in the Demo. Have you tried using it, instead of the last version of the Detour library ? Does the demo work with it ?<br><br>The strange thing about it is that a new version of the Recast/Detour library could make the navigation mesh (.bin file) unusable, but from your console it seems that the problem is related to the fact that the btBvhTriangleMeshShape of the .obj file is being added twice (see: btCollisionWorld::addCollisionObject(...)). Now I've no time to double check the code I posted right now, but I think I used something like: <div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>btRigidBody* groundBody = localCreateRigidBody(0,tr,groundShape);</code></pre></div>that, in turn, includes the addRigidBody call.<br><br>So: have you modified the code so that you add the groundShape to the world twice ?<br><br>BTW: I usually compile and test my code on Ubuntu Linux 64 bit only (without SSE support), but this shouldn't make any difference here, I suppose.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2180">Flix</a> — Sat Mar 08, 2014 10:51 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
